Error: Jet.UnconditionalRecursion: Every path through `ping` calls `pong`, and every path through `pong` leads back to `ping`, so no call of `ping` returns
  --> Tests/UILint/inferred_never_transitive.jet:23:27
    |
 23 | ping: fn(n: Int) -> Int { pong(n + 1) }
    |                           ^^^^
 Why: No path through the body reaches a `return` or its end without calling again, so the calls nest until the stack runs out
 Fix: Give `ping` a path that returns without calling again, such as a check on an argument that ends the recursion
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UnconditionalRecursion

